{% from "_macros.html.j2" import means, does_not_show with context %}
{% set L = iv.q4.leagues %}
{% set R = iv.q4.ratio_to_home %}
<p class="close-kicker">Question 4 · Czech hockey atlas · {{ q4.window }}</p>
<h1 class="slide-q">{{ cur.title }}</h1>
<p class="slide-a">Over {{ q4.window }}, skaters aged 20 or under played <strong>{{ pct(L.Extraliga.games.mean) }} of Extraliga skater games</strong> (95 % bootstrap interval by season {{ pct(L.Extraliga.games.lo) }}–{{ pct(L.Extraliga.games.hi) }}), against {{ pct(L.Liiga.games.mean) }} ({{ pct(L.Liiga.games.lo) }}–{{ pct(L.Liiga.games.hi) }}) in the Liiga and {{ pct(L.SHL.games.mean) }} ({{ pct(L.SHL.games.lo) }}–{{ pct(L.SHL.games.hi) }}) in the SHL.</p>
<figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q4-youth">
  <table class="fig-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">League</th><th scope="col" class="num">Share of games, mean (95 % bootstrap interval)</th><th scope="col" class="num">lowest–highest season</th><th scope="col" class="num">Share of ice time, mean (95 % bootstrap interval)</th><th scope="col" class="num">lowest–highest season</th><th scope="col" class="num">Seasons</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for name in ['Extraliga', 'Liiga', 'SHL'] %}{% set x = L[name] %}
      <tr{% if name == 'Extraliga' %} class="is-home"{% endif %}><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(x.games.mean) }} ({{ pct(x.games.lo) }}–{{ pct(x.games.hi) }})</td><td class="num">{{ pct(x.games.min) }}–{{ pct(x.games.max) }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(x.toi.mean) }} ({{ pct(x.toi.lo) }}–{{ pct(x.toi.hi) }})</td><td class="num">{{ pct(x.toi.min) }}–{{ pct(x.toi.max) }}</td><td class="num">{{ x.games.seasons }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Share of all skater games, or of skater ice time, played by skaters aged 20 or under (age = season start year minus birth year), by league and season, {{ q4.window }}; skaters of every nationality, regular season. How to read it: the Extraliga is blue, the Liiga ink, the SHL grey. The National League and the DEL are dashed and marked "not measured": they publish no birth dates, so ages are known for only about {{ pct0(q4.unmeasured_known.NL) }} and {{ pct0(q4.unmeasured_known.DEL) }} of their games, and their shares count only the young players who could be linked to another league. The table's means are unweighted means of the seasonal shares; the intervals resample seasons.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="q-evidence" aria-labelledby="q4-evidence">
  <h2 class="q-sub" id="q4-evidence">Evidence</h2>
  <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What was counted</span> Every skater of every nationality, regular season. A league-season counts as measured when ages are known for at least 90 % of its skater games; the Extraliga, Liiga and SHL are measured in all {{ q4.n_seasons }} seasons. Ice time is published by the Extraliga from 2013/14, the Liiga from 2014/15 and the SHL from 2009/10. The cut-off here is 20 or under (under-21 hockey); question 3 uses 21 or under and the goalkeepers in <a href="{{ prefix }}{{ qurl.q7 }}">question 7</a> use 23 or under.</p>
  <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">Ratios</span> The Extraliga's share of games is {{ f2(R.Liiga.games.ratio) }} times the Liiga's (95 % bootstrap interval {{ f2(R.Liiga.games.lo) }}–{{ f2(R.Liiga.games.hi) }}) and {{ f2(R.SHL.games.ratio) }} times the SHL's ({{ f2(R.SHL.games.lo) }}–{{ f2(R.SHL.games.hi) }}); of ice time, {{ f2(R.Liiga.toi.ratio) }} ({{ f2(R.Liiga.toi.lo) }}–{{ f2(R.Liiga.toi.hi) }}) and {{ f2(R.SHL.toi.ratio) }} ({{ f2(R.SHL.toi.lo) }}–{{ f2(R.SHL.toi.hi) }}). The same seasons are resampled for both leagues. In {{ q4.latest_season }} the Extraliga share was {{ pct(q4.home.latest.u21_games_share) }} of games and {{ pct(q4.home.latest.u21_toi_share) }} of ice time.</p>
</section>
{% call means() %}
<p>Across twelve seasons, skaters aged 20 or under took a smaller share of games and of ice time in the Extraliga than in the Liiga or the SHL{% if L.Extraliga.games.hi < [L.Liiga.games.lo, L.SHL.games.lo]|min and L.Extraliga.toi.hi < [L.Liiga.toi.lo, L.SHL.toi.lo]|min %}, and the 95 % intervals do not overlap{% endif %}. {% set g_sep = L.Extraliga.games.max < [L.Liiga.games.min, L.SHL.games.min]|min %}{% set t_sep = L.Extraliga.toi.max < [L.Liiga.toi.min, L.SHL.toi.min]|min %}{% if t_sep %}On ice time, the Extraliga's highest season ({{ pct(L.Extraliga.toi.max) }}, {{ L.Extraliga.max_season.toi }}) was below the lowest season of both other leagues{% if not g_sep %}; on games, its highest season ({{ pct(L.Extraliga.games.max) }}) was above the Liiga's lowest ({{ pct(L.Liiga.games.min) }}){% endif %}.{% endif %} The comparison is between league-level shares. It does not measure the opportunity a given young player receives, and the leagues differ in their share of imported players and in how often young players are loaned to lower leagues, which this measure does not separate.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% call does_not_show() %}
<li>Whether the young players who do not appear in these leagues are playing elsewhere (lower leagues, junior leagues, North America).</li>
{% endcall %}
